 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\n10. In the Node Category field, the corresponding category is selected. The node ID that you selected with a double-click is in\nthe Nodes field.\n\n11. Select a group in the Group Category field. This must be situated one level lower in the hierarchy than the group you have\n\nalready selected.\n\nee Example\nYou selected a season group as the first node under the component. The next node must be either a day group or a\ntime-of-use group. It would make no sense to allocate another season group here.\n\n12. Choose Transfer.\n13. Repeat steps 9 to 11 for every additional group that you want to arrange.\n14. Once you have defined all nodes for the component, save your entries.\n\n15. You have to generate the components before you can use them in the RTP interface. To do this choose Generate\n\nComponent Code.\n\n4\\ Caution\n\nOnce generated, you can no longer change the components.\n\nExample\n\nYou have defined the following RTP components:\n4) COMP1 Component 1\n SU Summer\n\n\u00b0 |@) WD Weekdays\no (4) 0-6 Off-Peak Rate\no (\u00a9) 6-21 On-Peak Rate\no (4) 21-0 Off-Peak Rate\ne |@) WED Weekend Days\no {%) 0-8 Off-Peak Rate\no {&) 8-23 On-Peak Rate\n\no {4} 23-0 Off-Peak Rate\n\nGF) WI Winter\n\ne (\u00a9) 0-6 Off-Peak Rate\ne (5) 6-22 On-Peak Rate\n\n\u00b0  \u00ae 22-0 Off-Peak Rate\n",
